# The Kabyle "sharp" that closes a whole-hour reading.
# "swaswa" = exactly, precisely ("d lɛecṛa swaswa" = it is ten exactly).
# kab.wikipedia uses it in running text:
#   "war ma nezmer ad d-nessiweḍ ad d-nini swaswa asmi i teɣli tneggarut-a"
#     (Tafsut n Yimaziɣen)
#   "Lqedd n iɣezzuba n tnezzut n temdint-a ur tettwassen ara swaswa" (Bgayet)
swaswa
# "gedged" is the second exactness marker, and rests on the native Kabyle
# speaker @athmanemokraoui alone.  On
# https://github.com/TigreGotico/chronologia/pull/846#issuecomment-5573978767:
#   "Also 'd lweḥda swaswa' or 'd lweḥda gedged' for 'it is one o'clock
#    precisely'."
gedged
